    "werewolf.a_werewolf": "A werewolf",
    "werewolf.someone": "Someone",
    "werewolf.power.little_girl": "At night, you spy on the werewolves: you read their messages and see their victim, without seeing who they are.",
    "werewolf.power.elder": "You survive the first werewolf attack. If the village kills you, it loses its powers.",
    "werewolf.power.idiot": "If the village votes against you, it recognises you and spares you: you stay, but you can't vote anymore.",
    "werewolf.power.scapegoat": "If the vote ends in a tie, you are the one eliminated.",
    "werewolf.power.raven": "Every night, point at a player: tomorrow, they start the vote with two votes against them.",
    "werewolf.power.fox": "Every night, sniff a player and their two neighbours: you learn if there is a werewolf among them. One mistake, and you lose your nose.",
    "werewolf.power.bear_tamer": "Every morning, your bear growls if a werewolf is sitting next to you.",
    "werewolf.power.knight": "If the werewolves devour you, your rusty sword kills the first werewolf on your left the following night.",
    "werewolf.power.sister": "You and your sister know each other: you can trust each other.",
    "werewolf.power.wild_child": "On the first night, choose a role model. If your model dies, you become a werewolf.",
    "werewolf.power.wolf_dog": "On the first night, choose your side: stay a villager, or join the werewolves.",
    "werewolf.power.big_bad_wolf": "You hunt with the pack, then alone: one more prey every night, as long as no werewolf has died.",
    "werewolf.power.accursed_father": "Once per game, instead of devouring the pack's prey, you infect it: it becomes a werewolf.",
    "werewolf.power.white_wolf": "You hunt with the pack, but you play alone: every other night, you can devour a werewolf. Win alone.",
    "werewolf.power.piper": "Every night, charm two players. You win alone when all the other living players are charmed.",
    "werewolf.power.angel": "Get eliminated on the first day (or the first night) and you win alone. Otherwise, you play with the village.",
    "werewolf.desc.werewolf": "Every night, the pack wakes up, chooses a victim together and devours it. By day, the werewolves sit among the villagers and pretend to be one of them. They win when only werewolves are left.",
    "werewolf.desc.villager": "The Villager has no power other than their vote. Listen, ask questions, spot the lies: the village wins when all the werewolves are gone.",
    "werewolf.desc.seer": "Every night, the Seer looks into her crystal ball and discovers the role of a player of her choice. Use what you know without giving yourself away: the werewolves dream of devouring you.",
    "werewolf.desc.witch": "The Witch wakes up after the werewolves and learns who they attacked. She has a healing potion, to save that player, and a death potion, to kill anyone she wants. Each potion can only be used once per game.",
    "werewolf.desc.hunter": "When the Hunter dies, whatever the cause, he fires one last shot: he chooses a player who dies with him. Aim well!",
    "werewolf.desc.cupid": "On the first night, Cupid chooses two lovers (himself included, if he wants). They discover each other's role. If one dies, the other dies of grief. A villager and a werewolf in love win together if they are the last two left.",
    "werewolf.desc.guard": "Every night, the Guard protects a player (himself included) from the werewolves' attack. He can't protect the same player two nights in a row. His protection doesn't stop the Witch's poison.",
    "werewolf.desc.little_girl": "While the werewolves choose their victim, the Little Girl peeks through half-open eyes: she reads what the pack says and who they choose, but she can't see who is talking.",
    "werewolf.desc.elder": "The Elder is tough: the werewolves have to attack him twice to kill him. But if the village kills him (by vote, the Witch or the Hunter), the shamed village loses its special powers.",
    "werewolf.desc.idiot": "When the village votes against the Village Idiot, everyone discovers his role and spares him: he stays in the village, but he can't vote anymore.",
    "werewolf.desc.scapegoat": "When the vote ends in a tie, nobody else is eliminated: the Scapegoat pays for everyone.",
    "werewolf.desc.raven": "Every night, the Raven can point at a player. The next day, that player starts the vote with two votes against them, and everyone knows it.",
    "werewolf.desc.fox": "Every night, the Fox sniffs a player and their two living neighbours. If there is a werewolf among the three, he smells it. If not, he loses his nose and his power for the rest of the game.",
    "werewolf.desc.bear_tamer": "Every morning, the Bear Tamer's bear growls (everyone hears it) if at least one of its master's two living neighbours is a werewolf.",
    "werewolf.desc.knight": "If the werewolves devour the Knight, his rusty sword wounds one of them: the first werewolf on his left dies of tetanus the following night.",
    "werewolf.desc.sister": "The two Sisters know each other from the first night. Two players who can trust each other: a precious help for the village.",
    "werewolf.desc.wild_child": "On the first night, the Wild Child chooses a role model. As long as the model lives, the Wild Child plays for the village. If the model dies, the Wild Child becomes a werewolf and joins the pack.",
    "werewolf.desc.wolf_dog": "On the first night, the Wolfhound chooses: stay a faithful villager, or join the werewolves and hunt with them for the rest of the game.",
    "werewolf.desc.big_bad_wolf": "The Big Bad Wolf hunts with the pack, then wakes up alone and devours a second victim, as long as no member of the pack has died.",
    "werewolf.desc.accursed_father": "Once per game, when the pack has chosen its prey, the Accursed Wolf-Father can infect it instead of devouring it: the prey survives, but becomes a werewolf, keeping its power.",
    "werewolf.desc.white_wolf": "The White Werewolf hunts with the pack, but only plays for himself: every other night, he can devour a werewolf. He wins if he is the last one alive.",
    "werewolf.desc.piper": "Every night, the Pied Piper charms two players. The charmed players learn who else is charmed. He wins alone as soon as all the other living players are charmed.",
    "werewolf.desc.angel": "The Angel wants to go to heaven right away: if eliminated on the first day (or devoured on the first night), the Angel wins alone and the game ends. Otherwise, the Angel becomes a simple villager.",
    "werewolf.step.wolf_dog": "The Wolfhound",
    "werewolf.step.wild_child": "The Wild Child",
